{
  "_comment": "Unit templates. domain: land (default) or sea (warships move only on open water). `symbol` is the terminal NATO-style map glyph, drawn as [symbol]: X infantry, O armor, • artillery, H HQ/logistics, m militia, D destroyers, B battle squadron, U submarines. Stacks draw as [*]. SPEED (one map row = 10 miles, config map.miles_per_cell): speed_mpd = sustained march in miles per day over open plains; truck_mpd = extra miles per day with a full establishment of trucks and fuel (scaled by the truck fill). Movement points per week = miles per week / 10; roads and rail stretch them (config map.transport_cost). detection_radius = rows. loadout: equipment carried at full establishment (ids in equipment.json). fuel_use: fuel_drums consumed per week by status. stances: combat multipliers. name_pattern: name for newly raised formations. upgrades: tech id -> extra establishment items once researched. modernize: tech id -> {old item: new item | [new item, quantity ratio]}: once researched the establishment switches to the new item and old stock is turned in as the new arrives. support (artillery): fires in support of friendly battles within combat.artillery_support_range instead of fighting in the line. hull_defense (warships): damage taken is divided by it. asw: hunts submarines. stealth: hard to detect. engineer (Combat Engineer Battalion [E]): a formation holding position inside its supply net repairs engineering.repair_per_week destroyed rail/road cells within engineering.repair_range rows.",
